 "seconds": 13.1,
 "text": "Brief reasoning for each question:\n\n1. A fixed mass of ideal gas has total kinetic energy that depends only on temperature → **C**\n2. International Women's Day is 8 March → **C**\n3. A duckling following its mother is imprinting, which is learned. The other options are innate behaviours → **C**\n4. In the Joule–Thomson effect the gas cools. The molecules use internal energy to overcome attraction, i.e., they take heat from their internal energy → **D**\n5. Cyanide is the potent poison → **B**\n6. 15.6 × 0.08 = 1.248 → **B**\n7. The Padma Bridge has 41 spans → **A**\n8. Magnetic force ∝ 1/r², so halving the distance makes the force four times larger → **C**\n9. Hormones are not mainly carbohydrates; they are proteins, steroids or amines → **C**\n10. IBM took its name in 1924. The company was founded in 1911 as CTR → **A**\n11. NATO was founded on 4 April 1949 → **B**\n12. Platinum is paramagnetic. Gold and silver are diamagnetic, and nickel is ferromagnetic → **A**\n13. 10% w/v NaCl is 100 g/L. 100 ÷ 58.5 = 1.709 M → **C**\n14. A sporozoite is spindle-shaped → **B**\n15. Boiling point rises with halogen mass: RI > RBr > RCl > RF → **B**\n\n{\"answers\": {\"9a6c7ccb-5629-4c39-b466-769d806e834e-91633\": \"C\", \"9bfe3d1f-c73d-4c27-94ff-0a339768b65a-117519\": \"C\", \"9d8eea52-2e9f-404b-be21-b87a708caf2b-77460\": \"C\", \"9e6edb2e-0313-4433-b91b-443b37f4f244-117451\": \"D\", \"9e7b4423-f37a-4aad-9ec7-519f171022fd-87768\": \"B\", \"9eb333a5-0073-400c-837e-2d9e09de977f-113467\": \"B\", \"9fa79bfa-fd6d-4f31-9c65-157cf2f3b9a0-87084\": \"A\", \"9ff58c7a-a58d-47db-b5d0-f6c67f71fcc3-146237\": \"C\", \"a025dc7c-65b4-45f0-837a-8c7e160091bd-104347\": \"C\", \"a0695693-6288-4611-b318-31976d953757-120894\": \"A\", \"a11b9d74-6205-4506-b621-dfa5ea20326d-13055\": \"B\", \"a27c1239-bb38-4b8d-8cc2-bade7839d4db-82941\": \"A\", \"a416285c-87e0-4ba5-a68d-27d0f7db1641-22086\": \"C\", \"a4a36766-7e11-4e80-840d-5b02e7b38a76-51803\": \"B\", \"a5e05b03-6edd-48d3-91a6-802be9979a05-